        <p>`• We mean business," said one of Her Meiesty'• Ministers the other day, when asked whether the recent speechen of the Commander•ln Chief end the Under Secretary for War were preliminary to pro- pomals for increasing the stningt h of the army. The night hon. gentleman declined to enter into lArtlCUllrx, but he a`lositted that the "busioesit" meant a not inconsiiiersble inureeo in the army I E.llllllLea. in the meantime the • Service Man, Anita" see in the speeches referred to a proof that their warnings to the Government, sod espe- . cially the collective letter which they addressed to the Prime Minister CoWards the end of last section, have aronsed the Militlkry •uthoritiee to an " ap- preciation of the situation" In 'hrs. warninge it wan contended that the speaker. of the home bat- talions and the impossibility if rending out any email military expedition without further weaken- ing them constituted a grew. national langer. Thin. be it noted, was after the House had passed est iniirtes for increasing the strength of the arm, by Per hettalinne. In the opinion of the Service Committee the requirements of the case could not be even remotely met by an addition of leas than eleven bath clione.</p>
        <p>The show of homing pigeons at 'lie Ati twine!, on Tuesday aroused much interest, a tart which may be ascribed to the Inc aaaa leg •slite of these saga- clone meseengers Sc emle.nrien in time of war. It wen • strictly" businese " dieplay,the right to com- pets, in the principel clans having been won by no ordinary ecliievemente. Thum in clans I there were but reven birds, but all hod Sown the IWO mitre be- tween the Shetlands end London. The number of birds staged was over 400. There have been larger ehowe, hut hirer probably • finer. The Judge, Mr. Key, went Cu far, indeed, S. to 'pronounce it • uni- que year fur" homers." The catalogue wee capital Ireading, full of tioeininhle record. as to distances covered by the occupants of h. cage..</p>
