        <p>t tappened one Saturday afternoon that a dvsolate rain was fulling, and a visit to Hyde Park would have been fruitless. Thorn would be 1111 carriages out. on a day like dos, when the gum. light. beamed in sickly fashion oil day in the shops, and • grey desolation brooded like • night. mare over the mighty town. Beryl's lire wee not lighted, The prioe of coo/ had gone up latterly, soil Mrs. Toploft, having reul an eaaay lir a ttttt wuentilie alarmist that the voial ileposits of England would at certain appointed date fail utterly anil a:together, had instituted a rigor... eioniany id cool in her lionschedd, nt order to put olithe day of national calamity. On livr return from Browse iek Simare she ate her luneheon—an unhuttered 1011. 'I lien she resumed her rubber overshoes, her long, shrouding blue waterproof earoille and cape, her round, grey straw hat, her glove* not umbrella, and went out again into the wet street.</p>
