        <p>The gni) of her preserver upon the horeis hit bad been a grip of steel. In carrying her to the stilewalk be Lore her weight with apperent esse, ea if she had been an Infant. He sat her tlown upon the walk, contanung tn upport her, for her fisee wu deathly white and she looked faint and iIL Her hat hung upon the hack of her need, her snull bead, covered closely with little red curls, waa bare, but ohs had never looked loveller than now in her terror and distress. Her transparent comp'. 1011, her big, vivid brown eyes glow-tug the aura, her tender, extimette mouth —all nude up • beautiful picture vs lovely as beauttful. Her resumer thought he had never seen • being half so lovely. "Are you fact ?" he uked. Let me take you into one of these shops," His ve was how and gentlemanly. lb ryl was collations of • feelnig of etti prise, and looked at Intra more eftroe.tly. She new • slender, toll young gentleman, with wht e lonic, a fair, liantl• *tune for, anti an our of well bred languor and indolence. Was this her ru•ner, whose quob. urong grip lull saved her (morn protulde death ?</p>
