        <head>WoMEN'S CFI AT.</head>
        <p>WoMEN'S CFI AT.</p>
        <p>In honour of the hirthday of Princess Ens, only datryliter rit Princes. Henry ot It atenberg, who has just completed her tenth year, an exhibit'ait of arlmared phot,raphs was given before the (7.•iirt at nalmoe.l on Illond.y 1.. t t.y the per•ougsl 11.stre n 1 it,. (j o. ri.. films dist,' y,t, incloded views taken of 11r, y and other m.rn her. f the Ror.i family in the High. lands, toc.h.r with, some remir.celoc. s ol Ile. D . . .</p>
        <p>Among the historical relics and war trophies at Wind- sor. which have been armor d in the cabinet. provided , for their reception, In this corridor between the Grand ' Staircase and the Master of the Household's offices, is a I helmet and coat n 1 eiminsnall, • Mandist flag with , oriental Inscription, from the Snudan, a Katibisti shield of hippopotamus hide. indent d with • sabre cut. George IV. silver piwder find, r rbes formerly worn by the King and Queen of the Sandwich Islands, a silver noun tureen and table anomie from the plate chest of the 32nd Regiment.da maned by a shot at ',Linton*, and an Abys- ainian crow n of silver and g,ld filagree. In a ease, partly occupied try nice of the spoils required by Sir Herbert Kitchener during the Dongola expedition, and presented to the Queen, is a Crusader's .word found In Wad /Inhere's house, and dating neat. the end of tiii I' toil century. Its two ridded blade aof beautifully,. mpeted and beam an inecripsion in Arabic, the English tend. if of which a" Do not draw me without resin,—Do not sheathe me without</p>
