        <p>Ina IN,lnatry in Plat in,. in tile me Electcaw. 1.1 whet might. without any violent stretch of the imaginetion, he dtecribed lut a miniature general electioia. The Karteley eleaitioe took pia m yesterday. Let the result Is not yet known. Then there in the eliaw tile for the Alehlleten lIIVINIOII, which will he decided moot Thuraday, the tontest in the Exchange division of Ltvorp, 41, while another vacancy has been crested of Deptford by the appointment of Mr. Di a.,: to the judiciel bench. In three of these cxeltsiats at %I eldleton, Liverpool, and Didionl the Ifovertiment is urn the defensive ii the full 114.11110 Of the word, be- cause the seats have lawn vaiwtel by 'nom, The resulte will be awaited with the keenest Intenwt. All the mallets will he bought on the strateet party linewand the decisiona tit the °teeters ought to given pretty reliable indication of the state of the political telt, A. for the Liberals have nothing to complain of. 1.. every constitnency ni which a contest has recently taken place, the party has rallied 111 3 !warmer which taught have seminal imposallolo 101011 010 disappointment and duprespiion of the general election are remem- bered. There is nil edit Mott thin is largely due to the weeknosa and blunders of the I lovernment. In fiche there hem 111.1. IL glaring breach of faith. A solemn promise which O. nipple to the frontier tribes has been shallielowly broken, and the rmillt is that the toiletry is involved in warlike operatiorm in which the army engaged no larger then the Ifeitiali fortma at Waterloo or the Crimea. In any event there is no reel honour to be gained from thin war, soil, considering th• nature of the ~ountry which has berm invaded, our troops run the risk of sustaining e reverse, which would seriolialy Impair British prmtige ei the</p>
